    q: 'What is PF-07258669?',
    a: 'PF-07258669 is Pfizer’s oral, small-molecule MC4R antagonist, developed to treat the appetite and weight loss of anorexia and cachexia. By blocking the melanocortin-4 receptor it lifts the brain’s brake on hunger. It is potent and selective, was efficacious in an aged-rat model of cachexia, and reached a Phase 1 clinical trial.',
  },
